ub would take; the command is what a reader\n470:       // types to run it, so it rides along only when the route names exactly one mode\n471:       // that has a command. A broader route leaves the key off rather than guessing.\n472:       const command = attachCommand(recommendation.skillId, compiledRoute, prompt);\n473:       return command && !alreadyOffered.has(command)\n474:         ? {\n475:           ...recommendation,\n476:           compiledRoute,\n477:           command,\n478:           ...(Object.hasOwn(TRACKED_COMMANDS, command) ? { policy: TRACKED_COMMANDS[command].policy } : {}),\n479:         }\n480:         : { ...recommendation, compiledRoute, ...(!command && routeNeedsMode(recommendation.skillId, compiledRoute) ? { needsMode: true as const } : {}) };\n481:     }),\n482:   });\n483: }\n484: \n485: // A typed command is the reader's own choice, so it outranks a routed mode: the\n[Output truncated. Continue reading with offset: 486]"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"limit\":20,\"offset\":466,\"path\":\".skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/handlers/advisor-recommend.ts\"}"},"time":{"start":1794558878638,"end":1794558879181}}}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794558879188,"sessionID":"ses_e2bf59bc7ffeU5sbEdqcp5ihjg","part":{"partID":"prt_1d40b6081001rliO8Q6ylOP6Pw","sessionID":"ses_e2bf59bc7ffeU5sbEdqcp5ihjg","messageID":"msg_1d40b4527001r1P78ZVYXZS6GE","type":"tool","id":"call_360fd8b3a6df44a498636b5c","tool":"shell","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"cd /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research && rg -n \"COMMAND_POLICIES|mutating|TRACKED_COMMANDS|NO_EDIT_REQUEST|DEPTH_WORDING|system-deep-loop\" .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/feature-catalog/cli-surface/advisor-recommend.md"},"output":"33:When a recommendation gets a `compiledRoute`, `enrichCompiledRoutes()` also asks `attachCommand()` in `lib/command-attach.ts` for a slash command and sets the optional `command` field when one comes back (`schemas/advisor-tool-schemas.ts:310`, `z.string().min(1).optional()`). `attachCommand()` names a command only for a `route` decision with `selectionKind: 'single'` and exactly one target, and only when the generated `MODE_COMMANDS` table maps that hub and `workflowMode` to a command. A bundle, a multi-target route or a mode with no command leaves `command` off. For `system-deep-loop` the prompt must also contain `/deep:` or a phrase from `DEPTH_WORDING`, so a prompt that only names a topic such as research or review gets no deep-loop command.\n45:`lib/command-attach.ts` is the single source for the values. Its generated `COMMAND_ROWS` block maps each id a scorer can return, whether the TypeScript id, the Python id or the entry id, to `{ command, policy?, ownerSkillId }`, and `commandRowFor(id)` reads it with an own-key check so an inherited name such as `constructor` never resolves to a row. `publicRecommendation()` in `handlers/advisor-recommend.ts` looks one up for the recommendation's own id and copies its `command`, its `policy` when present and its `ownerSkillId`, and it forwards the scorer's `kind`. An id with no row adds none of the three. A command attached through the compiled route takes its `policy` from `COMMAND_POLICIES[command]` because that generated table is keyed by runnable string, and it takes no `ownerSkillId` because the recommendation already names the hub.\n60:| `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/command-attach.ts` | Shared | `attachCommand()`, the generated `MODE_COMMANDS` table and the `DEPTH_WORDING` gate that name the slash command for a single routed mode. |\n","title":"shell","metadata":{"metadata":{"status":"completed","truncated":false,"exit":0},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"33:When a recommendation gets a `compiledRoute`, `enrichCompiledRoutes()` also asks `attachCommand()` in `lib/command-attach.ts` for a slash command and sets the optional `command` field when one comes back (`schemas/advisor-tool-schemas.ts:310`, `z.string().min(1).optional()`). `attachCommand()` names a command only for a `route` decision with `selectionKind: 'single'` and exactly one target, and only when the generated `MODE_COMMANDS` table maps that hub and `workflowMode` to a command. A bundle, a multi-target route or a mode with no command leaves `command` off. For `system-deep-loop` the prompt must also contain `/deep:` or a phrase from `DEPTH_WORDING`, so a prompt that only names a topic such as research or review gets no deep-loop command.\n45:`lib/command-attach.ts` is the single source for the values. Its generated `COMMAND_ROWS` block maps each id a scorer can return, whether the TypeScript id, the Python id or the entry id, to `{ command, policy?, ownerSkillId }`, and `commandRowFor(id)` reads it with an own-key check so an inherited name such as `constructor` never resolves to a row. `publicRecommendation()` in `handlers/advisor-recommend.ts` looks one up for the recommendation's own id and copies its `command`, its `policy` when present and its `ownerSkillId`, and it forwards the scorer's `kind`. An id with no row adds none of the three. A command attached through the compiled route takes its `policy` from `COMMAND_POLICIES[command]` because that generated table is keyed by runnable string, and it takes no `ownerSkillId` because the recommendation already names the hub.\n60:| `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/command-attach.ts` | Shared | `attachCommand()`, the generated `MODE_COMMANDS` table and the `DEPTH_WORDING` gate that name the slash command for a single routed mode. |\n"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"command\":\"cd /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research && rg -n \\\"COMMAND_POLICIES|mutating|TRACKED_COMMANDS|NO_EDIT_REQUEST|DEPTH_WORDING|system-deep-loop\\\" .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/feature-catalog/cli-surface/advisor-recommend.md\"}"},"time":{"start":1794558877825,"end":1794558879188}}}}
