{"type":"step_start","timestamp":1794558902435,"sessionID":"ses_e2bf59bc7ffeU5sbEdqcp5ihjg","part":{"id":"prt_1d40bc0a30015FMP1JBitnXBJ4","sessionID":"ses_e2bf59bc7ffeU5sbEdqcp5ihjg","messageID":"msg_1d40bb645001Ip3Eu7fD1vQrtP","type":"step-start","snapshot":"2f8d3bf51f84b03e7dc22733de44bedbafd07931"}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794558905592,"sessionID":"ses_e2bf59bc7ffeU5sbEdqcp5ihjg","part":{"partID":"prt_1d40bc0a50011XGr6yTbAOQGqd","sessionID":"ses_e2bf59bc7ffeU5sbEdqcp5ihjg","messageID":"msg_1d40bb645001Ip3Eu7fD1vQrtP","type":"tool","id":"call_0ad58fd2ec874dc79268744d","tool":"edit","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"newString":"to `{ command, policy?, mutating?, ownerSkillId }`, and `commandRowFor(id)` reads it with an own-key check so an inherited name such as `constructor` never resolves to a row. `mutating` is the class the renderer's child downgrade reads: `/doctor:env list` carries `read-only` and stays fully visible to a dispatched child, while `start`, `ask` and a writing `run` are marked as parent-named. `publicRecommendation()` in `handlers/advisor-recommend.ts` looks one up for the recommendation's own id and copies its `command`, its `policy` when present and its `ownerSkillId`, and it forwards the scorer's `kind`. An id with no row adds none of the three. A command attached through the compiled route takes its `policy` from `TRACKED_COMMANDS[command].policy`, the table keyed by runnable string that covers every tracked command, and it takes no `ownerSkillId` because the recommendation already names the hub.","oldString":"to `{ command, policy?, ownerSkillId }`, and `commandRowFor(id)` reads it with an own-key check so an inherited name such as `constructor` never resolves to a row. `publicRecommendation()` in `handlers/advisor-recommend.ts` looks one up for the recommendation's own id and copies its `command`, its `policy` when present and its `ownerSkillId`, and it forwards the scorer's `kind`. An id with no row adds none of the three. A command attached through the compiled route takes its `policy` from `COMMAND_POLICIES[command]` because that generated table is keyed by runnable string, and it takes no `ownerSkillId` because the recommendation already names the hub.","path":".skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/feature-catalog/cli-surface/advisor-recommend.md"},"output":"Edited .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/feature-catalog/cli-surface/advisor-recommend.md (1 replacement)","title":"edit","metadata":{"metadata":{"files":[{"file":".skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/feature-catalog/cli-surface/advisor-recommend.md","patch":"Index: .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/feature-catalog/cli-surface/advisor-recommend.md\n===================================================================\n--- .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/feature-catalog/cli-surface/advisor-recommend.md\n+++ .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/feature-catalog/cli-surface/advisor-recommend.md\n@@ -41,9 +41,9 @@\n ### Recommendation Contract (`kind`, `command`, `policy`, `ownerSkillId`)\n \n Each recommendation carries up to four optional fields that let a reader act on it without a second lookup. `kind` is `'skill'` or `'command'` and says which face the pick is, so a caller can tell a skill entry from a command row that scored as a candidate. `command` is the runnable slash string, such as `/speckit:save`. `policy` is `'run'`, `'start'` or `'ask'` and says how a caller may run that command. `ownerSkillId` names the skill that owns the command, which is the grouping key when several commands belong to one hub. All four stay optional in `AdvisorRecommendationSchema` so a response from a runtime that predates them still parses.\n \n-`lib/command-attach.ts` is the single source for the values. Its generated `COMMAND_ROWS` block maps each id a scorer can return, whether the TypeScript id, the Python id or the entry id, to `{ command, policy?, ownerSkillId }`, and `commandRowFor(id)` reads it with an own-key check so an inherited name such as `constructor` never resolves to a row. `publicRecommendation()` in `handlers/advisor-recommend.ts` looks one up for the recommendation's own id and copies its `command`, its `policy` when present and its `ownerSkillId`, and it forwards the scorer's `kind`. An id with no row adds none of the three. A command attached through the compiled route takes its `policy` from `COMMAND_POLICIES[command]` because that generated table is keyed by runnable string, and it takes no `ownerSkillId` because the recommendation already names the hub.\n+`lib/command-attach.ts` is the single source for the values. Its generated `COMMAND_ROWS` block maps each id a scorer can return, whether the TypeScript id, the Python id or the entry id, to `{ command, policy?, mutating?, ownerSkillId }`, and `commandRowFor(id)` reads it with an own-key check so an inherited name such as `constructor` never resolves to a row. `mutating` is the class the renderer's child downgrade reads: `/doctor:env list` carries `read-only` and stays fully visible to a dispatched child, while `start`, `ask` and a writing `run` are marked as parent-named. `publicRecommendation()` in `handlers/advisor-recommend.ts` looks one up for the recommendation's own id and copies its `command`, its `policy` when present and its `ownerSkillId`, and it forwards the scorer's `kind`. An id with no row adds none of the three. A command attached through the compiled route takes its `policy` from `TRACKED_COMMANDS[command].policy`, the table keyed by runnable string that covers every tracked command, and it takes no `ownerSkillId` because the recommendation already names the hub.\n \n The renderer and the degraded path read the same contract. `lib/render.ts` builds the brief label `<ownerSkillId or skill> → <command> (<policy>)` from the recommendation's own fields first and falls back to the generated row for anything omitted, so a hook that predates the fields still prints a runnable command. The CLI degraded path in `skill-advisor-cli.ts` emits a `kind: 'command'` entry with all four fields when the prompt contains the row's bare slash command, and otherwise emits the row's `ownerSkillId` as a `kind: 'skill'` entry so the fallback brief names a real skill instead of a raw row id.\n \n ---\n","status":"modified","additions":1,"deletions":1}],"truncated":false},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Edited .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/feature-catalog/cli-surface/advisor-recommend.md (1 replacement)"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"newString\":\"to `{ command, policy?, mutating?, ownerSkillId }`, and `commandRowFor(id)` reads it with an own-key check so an inherited name such as `constructor` never resolves to a row. `mutating` is the class the renderer's child downgrade reads: `/doctor:env list` carries `read-only` and stays fully visible to a dispatched child, while `start`, `ask` and a writing `run` are marked as parent-named. `publicRecommendation()` in `handlers/advisor-recommend.ts` looks one up for the recommendation's own id and copies its `command`, its `policy` when present and its `ownerSkillId`, and it forwards the scorer's `kind`. An id with no row adds none of the three. A command attached through the compiled route takes its `policy` from `TRACKED_COMMANDS[command].policy`, the table keyed by runnable string that covers every tracked command, and it takes no `ownerSkillId` because the recommendation already names the hub.\",\"oldString\":\"to `{ command, policy?, ownerSkillId }`, and `commandRowFor(id)` reads it with an own-key check so an inherited name such as `constructor` never resolves to a row. `publicRecommendation()` in `handlers/advisor-recommend.ts` looks one up for the recommendation's own id and copies its `command`, its `policy` when present and its `ownerSkillId`, and it forwards the scorer's `kind`. An id with no row adds none of the three. A command attached through the compiled route takes its `policy` from `COMMAND_POLICIES[command]` because that generated table is keyed by runnable string, and it takes no `ownerSkillId` because the recommendation already names the hub.\",\"path\":\".skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/feature-catalog/cli-surface/advisor-recommend.md\"}"},"time":{"start":1794558902437,"end":1794558905592}}}}
