{"type":"text","timestamp":1794558932192,"sessionID":"ses_e2bf59bc7ffeU5sbEdqcp5ihjg","part":{"id":"prt_1d40c2466002O5sPIQJ7PMoVZk","sessionID":"ses_e2bf59bc7ffeU5sbEdqcp5ihjg","messageID":"msg_1d40c065a001xByzTFEJ0Sn7Eh","type":"text","text":"T052 is complete. Only the file the task names was edited, and the checkbox was left unticked.\n\n## Files written\n\n`.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/feature-catalog/cli-surface/advisor-recommend.md` (2 lines changed, +2 / -2)\n\n- **Attach paragraph (line 33):** replaced the `system-deep-loop` sentence with one saying the prompt must type the same command or hold a `DEPTH_WORDING` phrase, and added that a prompt matching `NO_EDIT_REQUEST` gets no command from any hub.\n- **Contract paragraph (line 45):** row shape is now `{ command, policy?, mutating?, ownerSkillId }`, with `mutating` described as the class the renderer's child downgrade reads, and the `COMMAND_POLICIES[command]` sentence replaced by one saying the attached command takes its policy from `TRACKED_COMMANDS[command].policy`, the table keyed by runnable string that covers every tracked command.\n\n## Verify output\n\n```\n--- COMMAND_POLICIES (expect nothing)\nexit=1\n--- mutating? (expect 1)\n1\nexit=0\n--- TRACKED_COMMANDS[command].policy (expect 1)\n1\nexit=0\n--- NO_EDIT_REQUEST (expect 1)\n1\nexit=0\n```\n\nAll four conditions match the task: no `COMMAND_POLICIES` line, and one line each for `mutating?`, `TRACKED_COMMANDS[command].policy` and `NO_EDIT_REQUEST`.\n\n`git -c core.fsmonitor=false diff --stat` shows that one file only, 2 insertions / 2 deletions.\n\n## Caveats\n\n- Code cross-check: `attachCommand()` gates deep-loop on `prompt.toLowerCase().includes('/deep:')`, not on an exact command match. The wording I wrote is the one the task dictated and holds for the normal case where the prompt types the command whose mode resolved, but a prompt typing a different `/deep:*` command would also pass the gate. Nothing was changed on account of this; flagging it as an observation, not a deviation from the task line.\n- Nothing else was blocked; no installs, servers, sessions or commits.","time":{"start":1794558927974,"end":1794558932192}}}
